└──────────┴─────────────┴────────────────┘
```

**4 of 8 test methods are smell-affected. The other 4 are clean.**

---

## 🔴 High-Severity Findings

### 1. Sleepy Test — `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`

**Taxonomy:** testsmells.org *Sleepy Test*
**Severity:** High — Thread.Sleep introduces 3 s of wall-clock delay and non-deterministic timing. Even in integration tests this remains a smell (calibration: Sleepy Test is **not** downgraded for integration scope).

```csharp
// Line 87 — UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Fix:** Replace with a polling/retry wait:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with timeout instead of sleeping
    var timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
    var interval = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(100);
    var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();
    while (sw.Elapsed < timeout)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(interval);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification was not sent within the timeout period.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures on slow runners; 3 s wasted every run even when the notification fires in 50 ms.

---

### 2. Conditional Test Logic — `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`

**Taxonomy:** testsmells.org *Conditional Test Logic*
**Severity:** High — The `if/else` means one branch is never exercised, creating a hidden testing gap.

```csharp
// Lines 101-108 — UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two separate tests with deterministic setup:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscountRate()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0,
        "Premium user should have a positive discount rate.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** If `GetByEmail` never returns `PremiumUser`, the discount-rate assertion silently never runs — false confidence.

---

### 3. Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`

**Taxonomy:** testsmells.org *Unknown Test / Empty Test*
**Severity:** High — This test inserts 100 rows but asserts nothing. It passes even if every insert silently fails.

```csharp
// Lines 113-119 — UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion
}
```

**Fix:** Add a post-condition assertion:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    const int count = 100;
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(count, users.Count,
        "All bulk-inserted users should be persisted.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Complete false confidence — silent data-loss bugs pass green.

---

## 🟡 Medium-Severity Findings

### 4. Assertion Roulette — `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`

**Taxonomy:** testsmells.org *Assertion Roulette*
**Severity:** Medium — Four assertions with no failure messages. When one fails, the MSTest output shows the assert type and values but not *which property* was wrong.

```csharp
// Lines 35-38 — UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add descriptive messages:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be found after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip correctly.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip correctly.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Database should assign a positive Id.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Increased triage time when a failure occurs — developers must read source to identify which property mismatched.

